WEBVTT

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.900
You've already eaten, haven't you?

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.100
Go to sleep.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:25.900
C'mon, Shiratama, we've known
each other for a long time.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.310
I remembered something unpleasant.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.060
6 years ago

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:44.230
Skating first in the free skate
is Yukimitsu Mochizuki.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.850
Oh, Shinozaki!

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.560
Where have you been?

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.310
It's almost your turn!

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:00.440
I decided today's the day
I'm gonna beat you, so prepare yourse--

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:18.810
Why am I dreaming about that time now?

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.520
Episode 10

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.520
Finals

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.940
Now, we are here today at the
Grand Station Hotel Chane-Claire

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:02.520
to bring you the live broadcast
of the skating order draw for the finals

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:07.770
of the Boys' High School Skate-Leading
Grand Prix Series in two days.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.190
Bringing you the play-by-play
is me, Shinji Takai,

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.190
and I will be joined with
commentary by Noa Kuonji.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.270
Pleasure to be here today!

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.940
Today's your first day as a commentator, right?

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.980
I'll do my best to make it easy
for everyone to understand!

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:27.060
The skaters have all gathered here
and are waiting for the lottery to start.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.980
Now then, let's take a look
at each team skating in the finals.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.150
First, the team that made it to
the finals in the eighth competition,

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.190
in sixth place, Niigata Prefectural
Kogahara High School.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:42.350
Starting with the Emerald Noble,
the talented Himekawa,

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:46.440
it's a team that has been skating under
the same coach since they were juniors.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.230
You can't dismiss their strength as a team.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.060
What's this "Emerald Noble"?

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.600
Oh, it's a nickname I gave him.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.100
Kind of like a title.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.230
Right...

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:03.980
Next is the fifth place team,
Ehime's Matsuyama Fukuonji High School.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:07.650
It's their first finals appearance since
the team was created 20 years ago.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.350
It's like that saying,
"sharpening a sword for ten years."

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.940
They don't have any especially
outstanding characteristics,

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.020
but they all have high basic skills.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.560
Their style is to steadily rack up points.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:20.310
In fourth place is Saitama Prefectural
Ionodai High School.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:24.100
Their ace, Maeshima, has just returned
to skating after a five-year break.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.060
The Resurrected Young Red Dog, Maeshima...

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.020
"R-Red Dog"?

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:32.150
...and his teammates who can
compete at the national level.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:36.650
I'm already looking forward to the
performance they'll show us at the finals.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:41.730
In third is Hokkaido's Eimei
Academy High School.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:45.230
This team is also new to the Grand Prix finals.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.850
To place third overall as
relative unknowns is amazing!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.270
They're dark horses flying in--

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:52.020
I can't wait to see how far they can go.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:58.060
And in second, from Aichi,
is Chutei University Kamimaezu High School.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:03.770
As you know, the "perfect unison"
of the Ishikawa brothers is a thing of beauty.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.230
They have also become more
synchronized as a team,

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:08.480
so I'm looking forward
to their finals performance.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:13.770
Finally, we have last year's champions,
in first place overall, the Top of Kings,

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:16.190
aiming for their second consecutive win,
this year with Shinozaki--

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.940
Tokyo's St. Clavis Gakuin High School.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.100
There's no need for to explain, is there?

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.980
In addition to their Absolute Ace, Shinozaki,

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.810
and the Ruler of the Ice,
Team Japan guard Himuro,

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.480
all their team members have
proven how skillful they are.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:33.600
It won't be easy to tear down
their solid stronghold.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.020
Now, these are the six teams that
have advanced to the Grand Prix finals.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:41.190
Which of these teams
will be this year's champions?

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:44.060
The lottery to determine their
skating order will begin shortly!

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:50.690
I will now explain how the lottery will occur.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:55.100
We will have one representative
for each team come up to the stage

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.560
and have them all draw at the same time

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.560
from the boxes for the
short program and free skate.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:08.480
The numbers they draw will be
their skating order for each program.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.480
The rules and judging criteria
for the Grand Prix finals

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.150
will be the same as what was used
during the Grand Prix Series.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.770
Are there any questions?

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.810
Then, let us begin the lottery.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.440
Will the representatives for
each team please come forward?

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.400
I'm going.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.230
Okay.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.150
Do your best!

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.190
With what?

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.230
With whatever!

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:29.100
Well then.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.150
Right.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:35.810
No, not you two. The captain!

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.150
Have fun.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:37.750
Yes, sir.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.730
Good.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:43.560
First, please choose from the short program box.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:44.560
Go ahead.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:51.600
Next, please choose from the free skate box.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.020
I wonder how far Adachi's
team will be able to go...

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:57.690
Now, they've drawn from the free skate box,

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:01.310
and the skating order for the
Grand Prix finals has finally been decided.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.230
This is the order they will skating!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.190
Grand Prix                                            Finals Skate Order

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:08.690
"Saitama | Ionodai High School | SP 2nd | FS 6th "

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.940
All right, we're last for the free skate!

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.060
Why are you happy about that?

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.940
Doesn't it kinda feel good?

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:17.730
Everyone'll probably pay attention,
too, since we'll be last.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.060
It was decided by lottery, though.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.650
It's a matter of feeling. Feeling.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.770
Depending on what happens,
we can change our strategy.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.850
We got lucky with this order.

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:30.480
So, for the Grand Prix finals
the day after tomorrow,

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.400
we will proceed with this skating order.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.270
Thank you very much.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:37.650
Please give a hand to the
representatives from each team.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:48.520
Now, following the lottery,
there will be interviews with the skaters.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.350
Kuonji?

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:54.810
Right, I'll do my best not to lose
against the other reporters.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:57.600
Oh, Maeshima!

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:58.690
Huh?

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.810
The Red Dog is shy, is he?

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.560
Hajime and Susumu Ishikawa,

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.770
what do you think about
the finals skating order?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.310
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.520
The order doesn't matter.
The performance is everything!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.060
So, about that performance--

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:31.230
Will you tell us about what you'll
be paying attention to this time?

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.440
No, that's not what they're saying.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.230
Realize, Noa.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:34.310
Uh, actually, it's probably
better if you don't...

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.650
Hey, long time no see, Gen.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:39.060
Looks like you're working hard, as usual.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.270
Oh, I didn't greet you sooner.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:43.440
Hey, Himekawa!

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.440
Long time no see!

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.440
How've you been?

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:48.940
Sorry we couldn't go cheer you on
at the eighth competition.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.980
We had practice.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.980
Oh, it's fine...

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.100
Are you really that bad with Kuonji?

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.650
I don't want him to throw me off my rhythm.

00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:00.060
He creates this weird atmosphere.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.940
For a guy who took a break from skating
to come out shamelessly like that...

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.060
There's no way we'd lose to him.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.440
Hey, Terahigashi!

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:06.440
Huh?

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.020
You were working hard in Hokkaido, huh?

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:13.850
I'm glad I can compete against a former
teammate in the Grand Prix finals!

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:16.440
Let's both do our best.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.020
Don't touch me like we're friends!

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:19.440
It's not the same as before.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:20.770
Right now, we're enemies.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:25.850
We lost last year, but this year, we'll win.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:27.560
We'll be the ones to win nationals.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.710
That's a small dream.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:29.560
What?!

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:33.230
For us, the Grand Prix finals
are just a stepping stone.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.560
For the world championships taking
place three months after the finals,

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:41.190
every member of our team has been invited
to be part of the Japanese team.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.940
I'm not saying we'll all be
part of the starting team,

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:46.980
but it wouldn't be strange for that to happen.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.350
The Grand Prix finals are our chance
to show that we should be chosen.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:52.400
We have Shinozaki this year.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.280
This is our chance to vindicate ourselves
and become world champions.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.320
Himuro!

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:59.440
We're looking at a different
place from you guys.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.770
That's some big talk.

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:02.060
Did it rub you the wrong way?

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.270
Let me give you one warning.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.400
If you're looking at something too far away,

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.310
you'll neglect what's at your feet.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.940
Our training isn't that weak.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:16.150
Oh, sorry!

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:19.940
You two look really alike.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.520
Are you twins?

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.690
But this place is off limits
to the general public.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.650
You two stand out, so before you're thrown out--

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:28.520
Idiot. They're skaters in the competition.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.850
You skated against them in the first
competition of the series, remember?

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:35.400
We watched...

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.020
...the seventh competition.

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:36.650
Huh?

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.600
They talked?!

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.150
It's outrageous!

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.650
Disorder isn't the same as modulation.

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:43.650
You guys are just strumming
along based on feeling.

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:47.560
It might sound like music, and people
might praise it because it's unusual.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.440
But that's all it is.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.270
It's shallow.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:50.850
Your true nature will be unmasked right away.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.480
We are aiming for beauty!

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:54.350
As a team...

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:55.560
...supreme unison.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.690
That's skate-leading's...

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.420
...essence and...

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.150
...true nature.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:01.480
The reason for skate-leading's existence!

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.690
In that sense, Kuonji's team
is better than yours.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.770
Beauty and fun can coexist.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:09.730
There is beauty that's born from chaos.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.600
Can you elevate that into art?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:14.520
It's always the mavericks who change the times.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.100
People say that and disappear
without knowing their place.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.850
We know people like that!

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:19.850
We know a ton...

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.310
...of people like that!

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:22.030
Only a hero...

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:22.440
...can understand a hero.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.160
A disorderly...

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:23.650
...crowd.

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.320
Inferring the whole...

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:24.850
...from a part.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.310
Boys! What are you doing?

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.270
What was that about?

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:34.440
Sorry, Maeshima. Did they say
anything rude to you?

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:36.350
Oh, uh, no...

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:37.600
They do have a point.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:38.730
Huh?

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:41.230
Modulation or transposition...

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:43.520
We should be grateful to the unison
experts for what they said.

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:44.730
It didn't do any harm to hear it.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:47.440
They have nothing to do with this.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.810
The only one in our sights is...

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:54.270
The idol, Ms. Ito, said she was a fan of yours.
What do you think about that?

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.400
Many women have been talking
about how you have great skin.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.560
Do you have a special skin care routine?

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.270
What type of girl do you like?

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:02.900
What did you eat for breakfast?

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:07.440
Um... Please keep your questions
to those about the competition.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.730
Who let the entertainment reporters in?

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:13.350
It's amazing what you've done after
only just switching to skate-leading.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:17.150
There are still people longing
to see you skate in singles.

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.440
What do you have to say about that?

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:19.980
Idiot! What's he asking?!

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:21.480
No, he did a good job asking that.

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.060
Depending on his answer...

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:25.520
It could become big news!

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:32.400
At first, I switched to skate-leading
to expand my range of expression.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.150
But...

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:37.440
This is interesting in itself.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:42.190
To work together with my teammates
and match our performances--

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.440
That's something you can
only feel in skate-leading--

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.900
A type of expression that can
only come from skate-leading.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:51.650
I think that's the same
for all the skaters here.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:56.770
I can only perform like this with
this team... with these teammates...

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:59.850
It really is once in a lifetime.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:00.850
But...

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:02.150
But?

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:04.440
If I don't feel like I can get
anything more out of it,

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:08.650
I'll go back to singles and aim for the world.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:13.270
Do you mean, if you win the Grand Prix finals?

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:16.350
I plan on waiting until the
world championships, at least, though--

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.350
What the hell?!

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:19.940
I won't let you act so selfishly!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.480
I'll beat you--

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.810
<i>I'm</i> the one who'll beat Shinozaki!

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:25.940
We'll become the champions!

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.730
Yeah, everyone feels the same way.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:34.770
Beat <i>me</i> ?

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:39.270
This is the same as what I saw in my dream.

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:42.400
People say that, but no one
has ever actually beaten me.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:43.900
What's with this guy?

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:46.100
He seems different from earlier...!

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.020
Yeah, Shinozaki usually seems absentminded,

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:54.150
but when he focuses on the competition,
he completely changes.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.440
Please don't make me repeat myself.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.900
The other face he has that says,
"I'm going to be number one here"...

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:03.270
No, Shinozaki's true self...

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:06.150
The absolute king on the ice
who overwhelms everyone else.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:09.100
That's who Reo Shinozaki is.

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:12.230
None of you can ever beat me.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:28.880
Declaring the winner at the lottery!!

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:23.190
None of you can ever beat me.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.270
Man, that surprised me.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:28.900
This is his first time saying
anything like this, isn't it, Kuonji?

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.560
That's true.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:35.690
Maybe this shows just how much Shinozaki
is conscious of the other skaters.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.600
He never said that to <i>me</i> before.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.650
But with this, his intentions are clear, huh?

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:44.600
I'm already looking forward
to tomorrow's Grand Prix finals!

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:45.350
Yup.

