00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:53.690
All right, that's it for today's practice.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.600
Thank you very much!

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.770
Make sure you rest well after you get home.

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:00.230
Tomorrow's the competition.
Make sure you get rid of all your fatigue.

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:01.350
Yes, sir!

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.600
He seems mad.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:10.650
Yeah.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.650
Hey, wanna stop by somewhere on the way home?

00:15:12.650 --> 00:15:14.520
We finished early and everything.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:15.600
I'm going home.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.400
Just for a little.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.400
Maeshima, do you have a minute?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.440
Hm?

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.560
Sure.

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.850
What, really? Your treat?

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:31.690
Yeah, like a rally before the competition.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:32.940
Come on, it won't take long.

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:34.350
If you say so, Captain.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.350
Thank you very much.

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:37.100
What a kind father.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:42.600
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.850
Please tell me.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:48.560
I'm going home.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:51.190
Today's weather... was nice, wasn't it?

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:52.310
Huh?

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:54.690
I hope the weather's nice tomorrow, too...

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:56.190
What the heck are you talking about?

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:58.190
If you have something to say, then say it!

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.440
Or else I'm really gonna go home.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.020
Okay, I'll say it.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.560
Fine.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.810
I... hate you.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:05.730
Huh?!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:09.850
Wait, that's not it.
More accurately, I hated you.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:13.810
We worked for two and a half years
trying to win nationals.

00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:16.900
Just when we thought,
"This is the year," you came.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:20.600
As expected, you brought chaos to the club.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:25.270
But with your obsession with winning,
you also transformed the club.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:30.850
I feel possibilities this year that
I didn't feel in the Grand Prix finals last year.

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:33.100
So, I'm thankful to you.

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:34.850
For us third years,

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:38.400
this year's Grand Prix finals
will be our last high school competition.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:43.730
But even if we can't win nationals
this year, you still have two years.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:46.100
With the first years coming
next year, and a new team--

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:47.350
What are you saying?

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:48.690
Have you already given up?

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.690
No! I--

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.480
It's true, isn't it?

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:53.810
There's no next year or year after that!

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.060
You heard, too, didn't you?

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:59.440
If we don't crush Shinozaki in the finals,
then he'll go back to seniors.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:01.770
And Himuro was talking about the world, right?

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:07.850
This might be your once-in-a-lifetime,
first and last chance to beat Himuro.

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:09.730
Stop acting so half-hearted!

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.270
If you've got time to
cheer up an underclassman--

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:13.980
Is that how you speak to your elders?!

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:16.850
Why are you always so bad at things like this?

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:20.020
Even though you've been blessed
with so much talent...

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:22.270
I mean...

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:25.810
I've got my hands full worrying about myself...

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.940
Besides, I don't know what
to say to get you fired up.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.400
They're both so awkward.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:37.810
If you're going to be thankful,

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:39.650
then it should be after we beat those guys

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:42.690
and win the greatest victory together, right?

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:44.900
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:47.190
But at least be careful of what you say.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:49.230
Yes, sir.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:53.940
You were waiting?

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.190
Where's Maeshima?

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:57.440
He said he'd come after he called home.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:00.850
Sasugai already went, too. We should hurry.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:01.850
Sorry.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.060
About what?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.310
No matter what happens, tomorrow's the end.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.850
Let's do our best.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:10.440
Yeah. With everything
we've got, with no regrets.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:14.810
Speaking of which, does Maeshima
actually like chocolate?

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.560
That guy likes curry.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:18.770
Wait, but that's a meal.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.200
Shisen-en

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:26.650
Going running?

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:28.020
It's my daily routine.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.480
Don't get lost or anything.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:31.690
I'll be fine.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.770
Himekawa.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:35.650
Let us go with you.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.060
I can't relax for some reason.

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:41.230
Sure. It'll be about ten km, though.

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:43.100
That's too far. Make it shorter, okay?

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.230
Make sure it doesn't affect tomorrow.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:13.440
I was so surprised since he suddenly
started talking about seniors again.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:14.600
Did you know, Taiga?

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:17.560
No, but I had a feeling.

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:20.270
I'm also using him to get my consecutive wins.

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:23.270
It'll be good enough if he stays
through the world championships.

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.730
There won't be any switching back
to seniors or consecutive wins.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:27.810
Because <i>we're</i> going to win.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:32.060
But still, <i>we</i> will win.
I can't even picture us losing.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:35.730
That's how much confidence
I have in Shinozaki's abilities.

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:47.020
Good job, good job.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:51.100
Checking your position in each
part with loose movements.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:53.480
You're just doing minor adjustments,
but it looks more polished than that.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:55.480
As expected of my big brother.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:56.310
Hayato.

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:58.190
I came to declare war.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:01.480
Tomorrow, we're the ones who will win.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:02.650
What's with that face?

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:05.400
I'm tired of hearing lines like that.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:08.690
It's a necessary ritual.

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:10.400
This takes me back.

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:12.650
We used to skate like this all the time before.

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.650
Yeah, that's right.

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:34.560
Thinking back, that might've
been the origin of my skating.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:37.480
But as you can see...

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:39.480
I'm a decrepit piece of junk.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:42.770
I forced myself and rented a pair of skates,

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:45.560
but I guess it's impossible for me after all.

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:48.560
I'll make this the last time
we're on the ice together.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:49.650
Later.

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:51.940
I made my declaration of war, so I'm going home.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:53.850
Hayato.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.150
Thanks for coming today.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:59.230
I wanted to thank you before the competition.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.310
Huh?

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:06.230
Kensei Maeshima. Thank you for
calling him back and helping him grow.

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:09.310
It's really good motivation for me.

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.770
Oh, yeah.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:16.150
That's what I hate about you.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:19.770
How you only look at others as stepping stones.

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:22.020
I haven't felt like this in a while.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:24.900
I'm trembling with excitement
for tomorrow's competition.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:39.560
This time, I won't let you go past me.

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:47.230
Now, the competition to determine
this year's number one team in Japan

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:49.850
is about to begin!

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:53.350
The final competition of the Boys'
High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series--

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:54.940
The Grand Prix finals!

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:59.690
Which team will win the laurels of victory?

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:03.520
The fateful match is about to begin!

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:51.030
Next Time

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:51.030
Perfect

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:40.150
Wasn't Yukimitsu more
overbearing in middle school?

00:23:40.150 --> 00:23:42.270
He's been like this 
since we were novices.

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:44.560
No, there was a time 
when he shaved his head.

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:47.190
In college, I'm thinking I'll try
being a mysterious Russian

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:49.560
who can train snakes and hawks.

00:23:49.560 --> 00:23:50.850
Where are you 
planning on ending up?
